WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.824 --> 00:00:07.668
"Mrs. Sweet?"

2
00:00:15.654 --> 00:00:16.535
Maggie exclaimed.

3
00:00:16.555 --> 00:00:19.417
"She'd never steal anything from anybody!"

4
00:00:19.437 --> 00:00:21.598
"Yeah," Cole said.

5
00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:23.460
"Mrs. Sweet is great."

6
00:00:24.321 --> 00:00:25.101
Henry nodded.

7
00:00:25.121 --> 00:00:28.224
"I know you're new in town," he told Mr.

8
00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:32.690
Tate. "But everyone in Belltown knows how nice Mrs.

9
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:33.330
Sweet is.

10
00:00:34.231 --> 00:00:37.172
The Sweet Shop has been around since our parents were little."

11
00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:39.694
"Exactly," Mr.

12
00:00:39.714 --> 00:00:40.734
Tate said with a frown.

13
00:00:40.754 --> 00:00:44.256
"Mrs. Sweet doesn't want any competition from the Dessert Den!"

14
00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:46.557
"What makes you think Mrs.

15
00:00:46.678 --> 00:00:48.098
Sweet stole your flavor?"

16
00:00:48.398 --> 00:00:49.179
Cole asked.

17
00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:51.400
"That's a good question."

18
00:00:52.181 --> 00:00:53.281
Henry turned to Mr.

19
00:00:53.321 --> 00:00:56.723
Tate. "You haven't told us exactly what happened."

20
00:00:57.804 --> 00:00:58.840
"Oh right," Mr.

21
00:00:58.860 --> 00:00:59.441
Tate said.

22
00:00:59.461 --> 00:01:04.406
"Like I said, I invented a unique flavor of ice cream for the grand opening.

23
00:01:05.287 --> 00:01:07.348
I haven't told a soul in Belltown about it.

24
00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:09.130
It was top secret!"

25
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.032
"Then what happened?"

26
00:01:11.352 --> 00:01:12.093
Maggie asked.

27
00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:16.117
"Did someone break in here and steal the ice cream out of your freezer?"

28
00:01:16.137 --> 00:01:18.759
"No, nothing like that," Mr.

29
00:01:18.779 --> 00:01:19.320
Tate said.

30
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.484
"In fact, my ice-cream order isn't scheduled to arrive until this afternoon.

31
00:01:24.364 --> 00:01:29.028
But just this morning, I saw my flavor listed on the chalkboard outside the Sweet Shop!"

32
00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:32.070
The Lemonade Detectives exchanged looks.

33
00:01:33.111 --> 00:01:35.433
"Really? That's weird," Cole said.

34
00:01:35.453 --> 00:01:38.695
"It doesn't prove anything, though," Maggie said.

35
00:01:38.715 --> 00:01:42.378
"Mrs. Sweet makes up new flavors all the time.

36
00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:45.761
Maybe she came up with the same idea on her own."

37
00:01:46.862 --> 00:01:48.043
Mr. Tate shook his head.

38
00:01:48.063 --> 00:01:49.424
"I doubt it.

39
00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:54.249
How likely is it that she just happened to make up a flavor like bubble gum banana swirl?"

40
00:01:54.269 --> 00:01:57.090
"Bubble gum banana swirl?"

41
00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.110
Henry echoed.

42
00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.011
He and Cole had seen that flavor on the Sweet Shop sign themselves.

43
00:02:03.412 --> 00:02:05.172
It was one of today's special flavors!

44
00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.213
"Right. That's my flavor.

45
00:02:08.413 --> 00:02:09.973
See?" Mr.

46
00:02:10.013 --> 00:02:12.854
Tate strode over to the menu sign and pulled back the sheet.

47
00:02:14.154 --> 00:02:19.456
The sign said Dessert Den Grand Opening Exclusive: Bubble gum Banana Swirl Ice Cream!

48
00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.461
"How do you think Mrs.

49
00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:23.982
Sweet heard about your flavor?"

50
00:02:24.262 --> 00:02:25.043
Henry asked.

51
00:02:26.443 --> 00:02:27.384
Mr. Tate shrugged.

52
00:02:27.404 --> 00:02:29.926
"I assume someone at the factory told her."

53
00:02:30.987 --> 00:02:31.807
"What factory?"

54
00:02:32.087 --> 00:02:32.808
Cole asked.

55
00:02:32.828 --> 00:02:36.350
"The place where I'm having all my ice cream made," Mr.

56
00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:37.191
Tate explained.

57
00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:41.213
"I tell the owners what flavors I want, and they make it for me."

58
00:02:41.233 --> 00:02:45.496
"Mrs. Sweet doesn't use a factory," Maggie said.

59
00:02:45.516 --> 00:02:49.019
"She makes all her own flavors in the back of her shop."

60
00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:50.540
"She does?"

61
00:02:51.008 --> 00:02:52.369
Mr. Tate looked surprised.

62
00:02:52.389 --> 00:02:54.792
"Yes," Henry said.

63
00:02:54.812 --> 00:02:58.095
"So she couldn't have heard about it from the factory."

64
00:02:58.915 --> 00:03:01.317
Mr. Tate tugged on the sheet to cover his sign again.

65
00:03:01.338 --> 00:03:06.782
"Okay, I just thought of another way it could have happened," he said.

66
00:03:06.802 --> 00:03:09.365
"I've been keeping my menu covered up.

67
00:03:10.266 --> 00:03:13.729
But a few days ago the painter forgot to cover it before leaving for the night.

68
00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.072
Somebody could have looked in the window and seen it then."

69
00:03:17.944 --> 00:03:18.784
"You mean you think Mrs.

70
00:03:18.844 --> 00:03:22.446
Sweet sneaked over here at night and peeked in at your flavors?"

71
00:03:22.766 --> 00:03:23.346
Cole said.

72
00:03:23.366 --> 00:03:26.468
"That doesn't sound like something she would do."

73
00:03:27.508 --> 00:03:28.589
Henry agreed with that.

74
00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:32.090
But as he looked around the Dessert Den, he had a moment of doubt.

75
00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.291
Mr. Tate's new shop really looked great.

76
00:03:36.112 --> 00:03:42.174
It had a brand-new ice-cream counter, the cool hand-painted sign, and a shiny silver soda fountain.

77
00:03:43.495 --> 00:03:46.256
It was a lot fancier than the old-fashioned Sweet Shop.

78
00:03:47.168 --> 00:03:47.608
Could Mrs.

79
00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:49.710
Sweet really be worried about the competition?

80
00:03:50.711 --> 00:03:53.453
Maybe even worried enough to sabotage the Dessert Den?

81
00:03:53.473 --> 00:03:56.115
"No," Henry said out loud.

82
00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.277
"I can't believe Mrs.

83
00:03:58.357 --> 00:04:00.319
Sweet would steal your flavor idea.

84
00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:03.281
There must be another explanation."

85
00:04:03.301 --> 00:04:04.842
"Oh yeah?"

86
00:04:05.222 --> 00:04:06.183
Mr. Tate frowned.

87
00:04:06.203 --> 00:04:08.885
"I thought you kids were supposed to be detectives.

88
00:04:09.846 --> 00:04:13.669
The evidence is right there on my menu—and on her flavor board!"

89
00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.836
"Mrs. Sweet has the same flavor as you," Maggie said.

90
00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:20.078
"But that doesn't mean she's a thief."

91
00:04:21.539 --> 00:04:22.279
Henry nodded.

92
00:04:22.299 --> 00:04:24.640
"Maggie is right," he said.

93
00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.583
"It's just circumstantial evidence."

94
00:04:28.623 --> 00:04:29.603
"What kind of evidence?"

95
00:04:29.984 --> 00:04:31.164
Cole looked confused.

96
00:04:31.184 --> 00:04:34.326
"Circumstantial," Henry said.

97
00:04:34.346 --> 00:04:38.869
"It's evidence that implies something, but doesn't actually prove it."

98
00:04:40.229 --> 00:04:41.310
"Okay," Mr.

99
00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:41.890
Tate said.

100
00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.292
"So how do you explain what happened then?"

101
00:04:45.268 --> 00:04:47.070
"I'm not sure yet," Henry said.

102
00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:50.052
"We need to investigate and figure it out.

103
00:04:50.632 --> 00:04:51.793
We'll get back to you later."

104
00:04:55.857 --> 00:04:59.479
When the Lemonade Detectives got outside, they stopped by their bikes to talk.

105
00:05:00.981 --> 00:05:02.462
"You don't really think Mrs.

106
00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.883
Sweet is a thief, do you?"

107
00:05:04.263 --> 00:05:05.344
Maggie asked Henry.

108
00:05:05.364 --> 00:05:08.186
"Of course not," Henry said.

109
00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:13.350
"But it's really odd that they both ended up with that same flavor."

110
00:05:14.251 --> 00:05:14.972
Cole nodded.

111
00:05:15.912 --> 00:05:20.835
"Yeah. And it's not a common flavor like mint chocolate chip or fudge ripple," he said.

112
00:05:20.855 --> 00:05:23.177
"There's no way Mrs.

113
00:05:23.257 --> 00:05:23.978
Sweet and Mr.

114
00:05:24.058 --> 00:05:27.620
Tate both invented bubble gum banana swirl in the same week!"

115
00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.382
"I agree," said Henry.

116
00:05:30.402 --> 00:05:33.144
"We need to start our investigation."

117
00:05:34.284 --> 00:05:35.165
"How do we do that?"

118
00:05:35.485 --> 00:05:36.266
Maggie asked.

119
00:05:37.266 --> 00:05:38.687
Henry bit his lip, thinking.

120
00:05:38.707 --> 00:05:41.529
"I guess we need to go question Mrs.

121
00:05:41.589 --> 00:05:45.552
Sweet. Even if it's just to rule her out as a suspect."
